  {
    "group": "Nightmare",
    "level": 4,
    "name": "Night Hag",
    "flavor": "There are terrors that do not strike from shadows or from violence, but from helplessness. Night Hag is the art of becoming that ancient, suffocating force whispered of in folklore—the entity that sits on the chest of the helpless, draining life with every shallow breath. The vampire does not hunt with fangs, but with presence alone, sliding unseen into the mind of the sleeper.\n\nIn this darkness, no cries can be heard. No struggles reach the waking world. The victim's limbs fail them, their voice locks in their throat, and their dreams become twisted tableaux of asphyxiation and dread. The body believes what the mind endures. Slowly, the organs strain. Blood oxygen wanes. Cells starve. Sleep offers no refuge—only gradual collapse under the impossible weight of terror.\n\nFor the vampire, it is the most exquisite cruelty: a hunt without struggle, a kill without pursuit. Only the slow unraveling of breath, heartbeat, and sanity.",
