  {
    "group": "Quietus",
    "level": 1,
    "name": "Silence of Death",
    "flavor": "The world is a symphony of distraction. The rustle of fabric. The breath behind a whispered threat. The distant footfalls of pursuit. But when the grave calls, there is no such sound. Only absence.\n\nThe quiet becomes a weight. Their pulse quickens. Their breath feels unnatural. Even their thoughts feel hollow without the reassurance of sound. The universe has ceased to acknowledge them. In this forced solitude, paranoia festers, and the predator steps forward, unseen, unheard, inevitable.",
