  {
    "group": "Quietus",
    "level": 3,
    "name": "Touch of the Grave",
    "flavor": "The grave is not cruel. It is patient. It embraces without judgment, cradling flesh and soul alike in its formless silence. The ancient practitioners of Touch of the Grave do not strike; they beckon. They call the victim home.\n\nTo fall beneath this power is to experience a death without dying. All senses retreat. Sight, sound, touch, taste, even the weight of existence itself—erased. The victim does not scream because there is no mouth. Does not stumble because there is no ground. The mind floats in a still void, stripped of anchor or form. Identity begins to fray, shredded by absence.",
