  {
    "group": "Quietus",
    "level": 4,
    "name": "Forsaken",
    "flavor": "The Beast is the last refuge of every damned soul. Even as the body fails and the mind fractures, the Beast still snarls, still clings, still hungers. It is the thing that whispers survival into the hollow bones of the undead. But Forsaken tears that last anchor away.\n\nThe vampire does not simply attack. They reach into the coiled marrow of the victim's soul, and wrench. The victim feels the severing—an impossible sensation of being emptied from within, their monstrous will draining into nothing. Their hunger falters. Their blood grows thin. Their gifts wither in their veins.\n\nIt is not death. It is worse. It is emptiness. The terrible stillness where even the Beast abandons its master. In that silence, the victim stands hollow and powerless, stripped of the dark gifts that once made them more than mortal.",
