    "actionText": "The vampire must have already lifted the object using Shoulders of Atlas. This action is declared as the object is hurled.",
    "failureText": "As Success, but the object slips in flight. It strikes off course or glances the intended target, reducing the final damage dealt by half (rounded down). In addition, the Storyteller may introduce a dramatic complication: collateral damage, unintended targets, or property destruction.",
    "successText": "The vampire hurls the object as though it were any normally wielded weapon. Calculate damage based on the object's size and weight (ST discretion), adding the vampire's Strength score. Range equals Strength x 3 yards. Accuracy is unaffected by the object's weight, provided it falls within the vampire's lifted capacity.",
