  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Pillar of Self",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "The Pillar of Self is a mystical place of peace at the center of each chantry where magi may meditate to increase their inner calm and practice their eruditions. The Pillar comes with a hidden drawback though, as the Beast, initially chained by the Pillar, grows in strength while away from it.",
    "vitaeCost": 3,
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "3 Vitae + 1 Willpower",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "1 Full night",
    "successText": "Creating the Pillar of Self requires a nightlong ritual, with the difficulty determined by the location; the more remote and free from violence the location is, the lower the difficulty. A cave far from human populations that has never seen violence might be minus 1 die, while the site of a grisly murder-suicide in city would be minus 5 dice. Success creates the Pillar, which is conceptual rather than physical. The Pillar grants 3 bonus dice to Dominion rolls. If the magi gains 3 or more successes then they may choose to not to lose Dominion at all. Once a magi has created a Pillar, he must visit it at least once a month and expend another point of Vitae, or it ceases to function. In addition, for every week he is away from a Pillar, his Dominion rolls are at a cumulative minus 1 die.",
    "sourcePage": 200
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
