    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "The Witness of Whispers must be made as below. To activate the observation is instant.",
    "successText": "This ritual creates a scrying device which can be used to either observe enemies and events from a position of relative safety or hear sounds over a great distance. The ritual requires a three-inch pin, a length of thread, the claw of a raven, three points of the caster's vitae, a container, and one healthy human ear or eye (one or the other, but not both). The caster sews the eye or ear to the claw, and then seals the device in a container of her vitae. After a week has passed, the device animates and can now be placed in any location the caster wishes to survey from a distance. The claw allows the Witness of Whispers limited mobility and the ability to secure to any surface. To see or hear through the device, the user concentrates for five minutes and spends one blood point. Once a connection has been established, the caster may mentally move the device one foot per turn at will. For as long as the caster wishes, the device takes over her visual or auditory perceptions (depending on if she used an eye or an ear to create the device); instead of what stands before her, she sees or hears what the device sees or hears, but uses her own Perception. A Witness of Whispers has one health level and one dot in each Physical Attribute. The caster may deactivate the Witness of Whispers at will and may reactivate it anytime through following the above steps. It remains potent until destroyed.",
    "sourcePage": 201
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Scry",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "This ritual causes a body of water stained with black ink, a black tinted mirror, or a dark, rounded, highly polished stone to becoming a scrying device, able to center on an item that bears his psychic impression, or on a person or location. The object used for the scrying can be no smaller than a foot in diameter or larger than a well. The caster is able to see and hear as if she was personally there",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "If the vessel is already made, then only the su bject's blood must be poured into the vessel water, 1 point worth. If the vessel is not made, then that must be roleplayed first.",
    "duration": "Scrying lasts for one meaningful moment in a scene.",
    "successText": "The magi is able to see and hear from the water as if from remote camera, all that sulTounds a specific individual. The 1 point of vitae is from someone specific and it is that point of blood which is poured into the scrying vessel and water. Then the scene peers down upon the person as if being watched from a few feet away. Anyone within 10 feet of the subject can also be seen and heard. Further away, things quickly become fuzzy and muddled. The caster cannot use additional powers, such as Auspex or sorcery through the ritual. The person has a stark feeling of being watched but otherwise there is no evidence of the scrying power. Sanguis",
    "sourcePage": 202
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Serologus",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "In sanguine veritas. To a magi, all truth and power lies in the blood of the vampire. The power which flows through it holds more secrets than it has ever revealed. That which is known of a person, though, can been seen in the blood.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Perception + Investigation",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Perception",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Investigation",
    "actionText": "Instant",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The magi rouses their bloodlust and suffers their Bloodline Compulsion for the remainder of the evening.",
    "failureText": "Momma always let me lick the spoon.",
    "successText": "By tasting a single drop of blood, the magi can divine its origin. If it is vitae, the magi can discern the relative power (Generation) of its source, its freshness (how long it has been since the vampire fed), and concentration (how much blood the vampire holds). If the blood is mortal, he can identify whether or not it is mixed with vitae, thereby recognizing ghouls, as well as any blood- or humor-based illnesses affecting the mortal source. This taste of blood cannot blood bond the magi.\n\nsingle success can determine whether or not vitae comes from vampire of much higher or lower generation than the magi, with more successes giving more precise information. It takes at least three successes to estimate the concentration of the blood (that is, the size of the source's blood pool), and five successes gives detailed information on all aspects of the vitae. When used on mortal blood, one success is enough to recognize extremely ill sources or the admixture of vampire vitae. In the latter case, more successes let the magi know whether or not the vitae is from a source he has tasted before.",
    "sourcePage": 203
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Contract",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "This ritual creates an unbreakable agreement between two or more parties who sign it. The contract must be written in the caster's blood and signed in the blood of whoever applies their name to the document.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae (the magi) I to 10 Vitae (the signatories - the amount is chosen by the magi who seals the contract, each party signing the document loses this amount as per below.)",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "The signing of the contract in your own blood.",
    "successText": "Those signing the document permanently lose an amount of points from their blood pool maximum, which returned to individuals on a singular basis upon completion of the specific terms corresponding to them in the contract. If the document is destroyed before completion of the terms, the signatories can never regain the invested blood points from their maximum pool.\n\nThe choice to lose blood can be altered if the contract is to prevent some action. In which the stated amount of vitae is placed up for loss in the case the terms of the contact are violated. In which case, the vitae is lost from the pool of the violator(s) wherever they are instantly. This loss of blood can cause Torpor. If the contact is destroyed without a magi unsealing the contact, the contact will detail whom loses vitae.\n\nThis permanent loss does not apply to the magi who seals the contract with 1 point of their own Vitae (unless they are also signing the contract, in which case they must give up that much vitae as well as per terms above). Any magi who knows this ritual can unseal any such contract by spending I of their own Vitae and each of signatories spending the amount they would have permanently lost(this spend is not permanent.)",
    "sourcePage": 203
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Tempering",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "magi may instill vampiric vitality into an item drenched in her blood. Since antiquity, magi have made use of this power to conserve both common materials and the ancient relics of the house.",
    "vitaeCost": 3,
    "costText": "3 ofa Size category 5 item (+3 Vitae per Size category above or below Size 5)",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "However long it takes to coat the item in blood",
    "duration": "It lasts for a period of time based on the magi's Blood Potency.",
    "successText": "The item acquires a vampire's susceptibility to fire and sunlight, but it gains an amount of temporary Fortitude equal to the character's dots in Stamina. It also gains immunity to erosion by time or elements, such as wind and water.",
    "notes": "Potency Duration\n\n1-2 One night\n\n3-4 Three days\n\n5-6 Two weeks\n\n7-8 Three months\n\n9-10 year and a day",
    "sourcePage": 204
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Draught of Phoenix Blood",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "The story goes that if a magi can manifest this power, it is because she drank the blood of some long-forgotten mythical monster and it somehow changed who and what was. But since that taste, she has become literally unkillable. Anything that causes her Final Death will result in a complete resurrection, though she will be young, fresh, a new face and body, with only an incomplete picture of who she was. The only thing she recalls with any certainty is who killed her the last time.",
    "vitaeCost": 13,
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "13 Vitae + 1 Willpower (see Action below for details)",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "The magi must spend a point of Willpower and then each night for a fortnight; cover their body in the language of the magi, carved with a fine tipped blade. Upon completion the marks fade into a very faint set of pale white marks almost imperceptible to the eye.",
    "successText": "If a vampire who has performed this ritual is reduced to Final Death, no matter the means, she turns to ash that scatters like any other vampire. For a number of nights equal to the vampire's Blood Potency, she is dead and gone. At the end of that period, her ash gathers on the back of the wind or is pulled up from the soil and she is reborn in the body of one of her vestigium family members whom has at least 1 point of her Vitae (if multiples then it is Storyteller's choice). But this rebirth has a price.\n\nThe character loses a dot of Humanity (so Stains are gained), they increase their Generation by 1 (i.e. from 10th to 11th); to a maximum of 13th, they Burn 1 dot of Blood Potency (to a minimum of l). Any Discipline dots above her new dots in Blood potency are lost. All Diablerized Disciplines are lost altogether. All those who were Blood Bonded to her are no longer so. Anyone who had some modicum of her blood, be it ingested or stored, loses it as it becomes useless dust.",
    "sourcePage": 204
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Apanchomene's Song",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "With the slightest scratch delivering a dab of blood to mingle with that of the targets, Apanchomene's Song twists a victim's blood against him. The target's eyes swell and take a deep burgundy hue, muscles seize and veins bulge beneath the skin, and thin trickles of vibrant scarlet bleed into tiny rivers from all openings in the anatomy. This nightmarish affliction persists until the target collapses in agony or death throes, leaving no trace of attack.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Stamina + Larceny",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Stamina",
    "actionText": "In order to use this power, the magi's blood must first be ingested or enter the target's bloodstream, usually through drinking (even from a ghoul belonging to the character) or being pierced by a bloodied weapon. The character waits a minimum of one hour for her blood to be fully absorbed, entering the circulatory system to securely grip the victim deeply. After a moment's concentration, the magi calls upon this ritual to burst her target's blood vessels, intemally constricting the target's whole body by flooding it with ruptured hemoglobin that strangles him from within.",
    "dramaticFailureText": "Your blood the one who is focused as you lose your concentration. You suffer the effects of this ritual as 1 Lethal per botch die to you Head.",
    "failureText": "Your command of sorcery is poor, the blood within them forgets your name and you must find a new way to inject another point of your blood into them before you can use this ritual on them again.",
    "successText": "Your point of blood is used up and the target suffers levels of unsoakable Lethal damage equal to the number of successes on the player's roll to their Torso.",
    "sourcePage": 205
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Rapturous Touch",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "The magi absorbs blood through her skin, as long as she is in contact with the blood itself or an uncovered part of a vessel's body.",
    "vitaeCost": 0,
    "costText": "None",
    "dicePoolText": "Stamina + Empathy",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Stamina",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Empathy",
    "actionText": "Instant",
    "dramaticFailureText": "You lose a point of Vitae per botch die as the sorcery unravels in your hand.",
    "failureText": "You fail the incantations and may not try again this scene.",
    "successText": "With a touch, any part of the vampire's hand, she may absorb blood through osmosis. Regardless of Generation, she may only absorb I blood point per second. All the standard risks from drinking blood still apply (blood bond, poisoning, etc.).",
    "sourcePage": 205
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Frozen Form",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "Little is more terrifying to any vampire than letting a magi get a hold of their blood. With this, the magi can prevent the use of their blood.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Manipulation 4- Persuasion",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Manipulation",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Persuasion",
    "actionText": "Instant",
    "duration": "1 scene or 1 hour per dot in magi's Blood Potency, whoever ends first.",
    "dramaticFailureText": "You lost control of the sorcery and you lost a number of Vitae equal to the number of Botch die you got in addition to the I you spent to cast the sorcery.",
    "failureText": "The blood point I wasted and you may not try again this scene.",
    "successText": "The magi must have ingested at least 1 point of the target's vitae. The target is unable to spend any Vitae from the Blood Pool (though external source may still be utilized if applicable) for the duration of the ritual.",
    "sourcePage": 205
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Debitum",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "Terrifying to behold, Debitum demonstrates one of the most frightening aspects of sorcery: the ability to distill the essence of what magi refer to as the \"heart's blood,\" the holy or unholy life force that contains a being's soul.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "Functioning even on mortals, the magi must exsanguinate his victim of all but one blood point. He then pricks his finger and marks the victim's bare chest, near the heart, with speck of his vitae. He spends one blood point, spurring the speck of vitae to seep into the target's skin. Five hours later the blood ha fully found its way to the heart. The vampire tears open the victim's breast, moving past the rib cage to extract the heart. The vampire's own blood has calcified the heart into a semi-translucent grayish-white flask known as a \"Debitum\", the \"heart's-blood\" of the victim — which, if examined in detail, can be seen encased within, swimming in despair.",
    "duration": "Heart's-blood preserved in this way endures indefinitely.",
    "successText": "If vampiric fangs pierce it, the heart reanimates, pumping cupful of celadon-colored, aqueous, non-burning flame vaguely resembling the victim into the vampire's maw. If the victim is a vampire, upon devouring the essence, the drinker reaps all benefits and potential pitfalls of successfully diablerizing the victim. If the drinker is a mortal, they gain all the benefits of ingesting vampire blood without any chance of Blood Bond. A Debitum crumbles to ash if left vulnerable to fire or sunlight, or when emptied of its contents. Koldun You are a force of mystical will, taught how to wield your desires to bend and shape reality to your designs.\n\nYou may only use thaumaturgy if you have recently fed off a mortal magi or have access to the blood of a mortal magi (be it in container or by cutting their wrist). Mortal magi blood ingested recently counts as your entire blood pool worth. Anything external is counted as per its container size or how much the person has in them when you rip them open. OR Instead, if you use the blood of a mortal magi as an erudition you don't gain Antipathia.\n\nUnlike other rituals, this has a rating of 1 through 5. Each 10xp spent increased the dots you have in Thaumaturgy by l. (maybe get new domain and I new art each dot?)\n\nBlood you use that has a Passion related to the spell you are casting counts as an Eruditon.\n\nChoose your Domain of power: Regeneration (heal and repair) Destruction (destroy and burn) Protection (make tougher or harder to find) Alteration (change shape or function)\n\nChoose 3 Arts which define aspects of your knowledge of your Domain: Affect self Affect other undead Affect other living Affect inanimate Affect area Affect at distance\n\nDescribe a Method by which you have been taught to focus your mind and practice your sorcery.\n\nThe rating by which you are able to pull upon power from blood is Blood Potency\n\nYou have a pool of bonus dice you can spend from called Vitae which is equal to your dots in Blood Potency.\n\nYou may perform Eruditions when calling upon thaumaturgies to gain bonus dice to casting",
    "sourcePage": 206
  },
  {
    "group": "Hekate",
    "name": "Invoke a Spell",
    "category": "Chantry",
    "flavor": "You can call upon a narrative effect which thematically relates to your Domain and its effects matches an Art - if the Storyteller agrees, you may roll to cast the spell. When you draw upon blood sorcery to manifest power, Spend 1 Vitae and say what you want to have happen and how you go about casting it. Roll Thaumaturgy + Vitae (if any are spent additional) + Eruditions (if any) (no Willpower may be used). The amount of successes you gain on the roll is how much the subject is affected (how many points of damage a wound is healed, how much might you give yourself in Potence, how much a person's dice pool is reduced from being crushed by the despair of their life, etc etc) It has an instant effect and is done. A point of Willpower can make it last an entire scene if appropriate.\n\nEvery time you cast a spell you gain Antipathia equal to the number of successes you gained upon your casting roll. Once your Antipathia reaches 10, it clears out and you suffer the Dark Retribution. If you ever Botch a spell roll, your Antipathia clears out and you immediately suffer the Dark Retribution.\n\nYou may reduce Antipathia by: Oblations: You destroy or murder something of meaning, value, or aid to your character or someone in their life (relics, blood something of symbolic significance to your Method, etc.) and reduce Antipathia by 3.\n\nAntipathia Roll 1d10 to see which of these results apply your character. It is up to the Storyteller to work within the fiction and set of circumstances in which you garnered the Antipathia for your hubris. l) Manic: Your Flaws affect you far worse than normal. Now, at any given chance, your Flaw affects you as worst it can. This asts until the rising of the sun on the next night and an additional number of nights for every point of Vitae you spent to cast the spell. 2) Backlash: You take a number of points of Lethal damage equal to the number of Antipathia you just gained, plus any extra Vitae you used. If you Botched the roll, then the damage type is Aggravated. This damage can be assigned to any location and take the bloody form the player describes. 3) Madness: Your mind is broken as you see the infinite permutations of reality and any form it could have taken. You see visions of a warped world, of shattered realities and the voices of the endless abyss of death. Burn a dot of Intelligence. 4) Haunted: Your magi has torn the veil between themselves and a spirit world. For I day per dot in Blood Potency you have, spirits of all kinds are drawn to you and tear, scream, plead, thrash, and otherwise terrorize your magi. During this time if you do not succeed in a Wits + Resolve roll, you are at a minus to all you do equal to every point of Vitae you spent to cast the spell until the next sunrise when, if you are still affected, you may roll again. 5) 6) 7) 8) 9) 10)",
    "sourcePage": 207
  },
  {
    "group": "Vishap",
    "name": "Decay",
    "category": "Maleficence",
    "flavor": "This ritual ages an inanimate object, causing it to rust, break down or begin to corrode.",
    "vitaeCost": 2,
    "costText": "2 Vitae +1 Vitae per minute",
    "dicePoolText": "Stamina + Crafts",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Stamina",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Crafts",
    "actionText": "May only be performed once per scene. May only be performed on inanimate objects (will not work on anything in a state of 'alive' or 'undead'). The magi must touch the item to be decayed <insert how to use the blood in a",
    "castingDuration": "2 Seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "Whichever body part the lich used to touch what they wished to decay, its self instead decays as per this ritual. (i.e. their hand starts to crack and rot and turn to ashen dust.)",
    "failureText": "\"I like this, touching it gives me a sense of how old I am.\" Nothing happens.",
    "successText": "Every minute the lich touches an object and spends a Blood Point, the object ages 100 years. The max amount of minutes they can age an item is equal to their Blood Potency. Items will age as if they are lasting that duration in the current environment they are in. So iron may not change much, but wood may rot, or tapestries may become brittle or crumble, fittings and joints may crack or split. The item's patina will certainly look that old, and any scientific tests for the item's age will verify it's now older age, but will detect hints of unidentifiable manipulation that reduce its age credence.",
    "sourcePage": 208
  },
  {
    "group": "Vishap",
    "name": "Gnarled Wood",
    "category": "Maleficence",
    "flavor": "This power warps and bends any wooden object the Tzimisce sees into any shape the lich can form with their hands as if the wood were clay.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae per 501bs of wood",
    "dicePoolText": "Intelligence + Arts",
