    "sourcePage": 221
  },
  {
    "group": "Noctis",
    "name": "Shadow Play",
    "category": "Dark Reflections",
    "flavor": "This power grants the vampire a limited control over shadows and other ambient darkness. Though the vampire cannot truly create\" darkness, she can overlap and stretch existing shadows, creating patches of gloom.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Wits + Expression",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Wits",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Expression",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "duration": "1 Scene",
    "castingDuration": "3 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "none",
    "failureText": "none",
    "successText": "Vampires cloaking themselves in shadow gain an extra die in their Stealth dice pools, and add one to their Defense from ranged weapon attacks against them. Vampires using this power to make themselves more terrifying gain an additional die to intimidation Persuasion rolls.",
    "sourcePage": 221
  },
  {
    "group": "Noctis",
    "name": "Tenebrous Form",
    "category": "Dark Reflections",
    "flavor": "This power allows Vampires to separate shadows from their casting bodies and even shape darkness into the shadows of things that are not truly there. Once a Vampire takes control of darkness or shadow, it gains a mystical tangibility while under the vampire's manipulation. By varying accounts cold or hellishly hot and cloying, the darkness may be used to aggravate or even smother victims.",
    "vitaeCost": 2,
    "costText": "2 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Dexterity + Crafts",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Dexterity",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Crafts",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "castingDuration": "2 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The shadows are clumsy and move so slowly as to be unable to catch anything, they fall back to their natural state and the power fails.",
    "failureText": "Perhaps shadows don't like to be tickled..",
    "successText": "A successful roll holds or moves the shadow where and as quickly as the vampire wants, if the number of successes is greater than the opponents Defense then the Shadow may be used to follow or 'stick' to them regardless of their movements. In addition the shadow may be shaped in any way the vampire sees fit; they may even detach it from its casting source and move it up to 10 yards away. Opponent's plagued by flapping shadows and strangling darkness lose one point of Defense while in the shadow. Only one target may be affected by this power at a time.",
    "sourcePage": 222
  },
  {
    "group": "Noctis",
    "name": "Shroud of Night",
    "category": "Dark Reflections",
    "flavor": "The vampire can create a cloud of inky blackness. The cloud completely obscures light and even sound to some extent. Those who have been trapped within it (and survived) describe the cloud as viscous and unnerving. This physical manifestation lends credence to the talks of those who claim the darkness is more than mere shadow. The tenebrous cloud may even move slowly, if the creating vampire do wishes, though they must have total focus and concentration while doing so.",
    "vitaeCost": 2,
    "costText": "2 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Stamina + Stealth",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Stamina",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Stealth",
    "actionText": "The magi takes the blood for this ritual and spits or casts it into the air, whereupon it begins to take the form of an inky cloud.",
    "castingDuration": "5 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The vampires' eyes turn the deepest black and they are blinded for the rest of the scene.",
    "failureText": "Funny, the lights are still on.",
    "successText": "Darkness is generated roughly 10 feet in diameter, though the amorphous cloud constantly shifts and undulates, sometimes even extending shadowy tendrils. Each additional success doubles the diameter of the cloud (though at any point the vampire may voluntarily reduce the size of the cloud to a minimum of 10 feet) The cloud may be invoked at a distance of up to 50 yards, though creating darkness outside the vampires line of sight is not possible.\n\nThe inky mass actually extinguishes small light sources such as candles, lighters and hand held torches, but never anything larger (though it can put out a vampire who is on fire instantly). And it muffles sounds to the point of being indistinguishable. Those within the cloud lose all sense of sight and feel as though they've been immersed in pitch. Sound also warps and distorts within the cloud. Additionally the cloud reduces Stamina by two dots as it smothers air-breathing victims. Any breathing creature reduced to O Stamina begins to asphyxiate. In addition it reduces all creatures Defense inside the cloud by 2.",
    "sourcePage": 222
  },
  {
    "group": "Noctis",
    "name": "Arms of the Abyss",
    "category": "Dark Reflections",
    "flavor": "Refining his control over the darkness, the Vampire can create prehensile tentacle that emerge from the patches of darkness. These tentacles may grasp, restrain and constrict foes.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae per tendril",
    "dicePoolText": "Manipulation + Brawl",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Manipulation",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Brawl",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "castingDuration": "3 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "Tendrils of shadow erupt from the vampires' body and begin to constrict him. Each botch die dies 1 level of lethal damage as bones are broken and flesh is torn.",
    "failureText": "Nothing? Hmm..",
    "successText": "The tentacles sprout from any nearby shadow source, and in the case of a dark room, they may originate from any point the casting vampire wishes. From that point they are rooted in place. Each tentacle is ten feet long and possesses the following dice pools: Attack to grab: Equal to casting vampires Dexterity + Brawl Attack to crush once grabbed: Equal to casting vampires Strength Stamina Attack to lash/whip: Equal to casting vampires Dexterity 4 Wits",
    "notes": "Note: once grabbed an opponent is considered to have a defense and movement of O.\n\nEach tentacle has four health levels + number of successes on the casting roll. Any type of damage that fills its health chart disperses the shadow. However for a point of temporary Willpower the vampire may bring it immediately back in any valid location.",
    "sourcePage": 223
  },
  {
    "group": "Noctis",
    "name": "Black Metamorphosis",
    "category": "Dark Reflections",
    "flavor": "At this level, the kindred's mastery of darkness is so extensive that she may simply become it. Upon activation of this power, the vampire becomes an inky, amoeboid patch of shadow. Vampires in this form may slither through cracks and crevices and see in utter darkness perfectly well, in addition to Obtenebration created darkness.",
    "vitaeCost": 3,
    "costText": "3 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "castingDuration": "1 second",
    "successText": "While in this form the vampire is immune to all forms of physical harm save Fire and Sunlight. The range in which a vampire can move in this from is a radius from the point at which they activated the power. From that center point they may move as a shadow up to 30 meters. The speed at which they move is not affected by Celerity. General speed is considered to be a maximum of 30ft/sec.\n\nThe character becomes a shadow in a literal sense; somewhat two dimensional and able to not only move about but hear and listen and see as well. Though they may not themselves attack, if surrounding a mortal, the vampire can feed from them without penetrating the skin with fangs.\n\nThey may add +2 dice to any action using Arms of the Abyss while in this form, plus they may manifest an additional Arm for free when using Arms of the Abyss in this form. So it may very well appear the vampire shadow is attacking their victim.\n\nWhile in this form a vampire may roll his Charisma + Expression to mimic any shadow shape that can be cast about the area he is in. Such as appearing as someone else's shadow, or appearing as the shadow of a great and horrible beast, or even as an inanimate object. He simply need gain more successes than the observers Wits + Perception score. Should he fail the roll he assumes the desired shape more or less, but gives away his unnatural demeanor in some fashion, such as moving incorrectly or out of sync with the shadow casters form. Should he succeed then the observer is fooled in all ways of standard detection, only an observers Auspex Perception that is higher than the shadow vampires Obtenebration + Charisma may spend a willpower point to see through the sham. Vampires in this form may slither up walls and through vents; however they need a surface to attach to.",
    "sourcePage": 223
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Summon Soul",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "The power of Summon Soul allows a necromancer to call a ghost back from the Underworld, though for conversation purposes only. In order to petform this feat, the vampire must meet certain conditions: The necromancer must know the name of the Shade in question, though an image of the deceased will suffice The necromancer must gain as many or more successes as the Shade has in Pathos",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Charisma + Empathy",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Charisma",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Empathy",
    "actionText": "Slice your palm deep, and bleed enough Vitae onto the ground to feel the Sorcery stir; call out to the spirit by its name holding its fetter, and it will appear.",
    "castingDuration": "1 minute",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The summoner contacts a malevolent spirit which seeks to torment the summoner for her folly.",
    "failureText": "You hear something? See the curtain move? No? huh..",
    "successText": "The number of successes on the roll indicates the tractability of the summoned spirit and how long the summoned Shade remains in the vicinity of her summoner. Summoned ghosts are only visible and audible to the vampire who summoned them, and remain so up until the time of summoning wears off. Ghosts who wish to be summoned can voluntarily appear. For each question the vampire asks the summoned spirit, the Storyteller should roll one die per summoning success. At least one success is needed on this second roll in order to keep the spirit around long enough to answer the question.",
    "sourcePage": 224
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Compel Soul",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "With this power, a vampire can command a ghost to do his bidding for a while. Compel is a perilous undertaking and when used improperly, can endanger vampire and Shade alike.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Manipulation + Persuasion (needing more successes than the Ghost has dots in Pathos). Some ghosts can spend Pathos to combat the compulsion; each point spent removes one of the vampire's successes. The vampire may attempt this multiple times during a single summoning.",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Manipulation",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Persuasion",
    "actionText": "As with simple summoning, slice the palm, and then cast your Vitae ahead of you as if in offering to the spirit; it has no need for it, but intent is important.",
    "duration": "Compel holds a ghost for one hour per success. If the vampire wishes, she can expend a temporary point of Willpower to keep the Shade under the compulsion for and extra night. The expenditure of a permanent Willpower point binds the Shade to the vampire for a year and a day.",
    "castingDuration": "1 second",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The Shade becomes irate at the idea of serving such a fool, the summoner is at a -2 dice penalty in taking any action to defend or attack the Shade for the rest of the scene.",
    "failureText": "She had such beautiful eyes.",
    "successText": "For each success achieved, the necromancer achieves a greater degree of control over the Shade as follows:",
    "notes": "Prerequisite: You must first have Summon Soul before you can purchase this ritual. And you must first Summon a Shade before you can use any of this ritual.\n\n1-2 success The Shade must remain in the vicinity and refrain from attacking any creature without the necromancer's consent. And is to answer any questions truthfully though it may omit or evade answers, though the questions need be phrased carefully. It does not have to obey the necromancer to petform any commanded tasks. 3-4 successes The Shade is forced to remain and answer any questions truthfully, without evasion or omission. It must also perform any services commanded by its new master, though it is bound only by the letter of the command, not the spirit. successes The Shade remains, and obeys the spirit of the necromancer's commands to the best of its ability. The Shade is able to be Soul Trapped if the necromancer knows how and has the right items.",
    "sourcePage": 224
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Haunting",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "Haunting binds a summoned ghost to a particular location or, in extreme cases, and object. The Shade cannot leave the area to which the necromancer binds it without risking self-destruction. Shade attempting to leave the area of the haunting must make Willpower roll needing two successes or take a level of aggravated damage. If the Shade loses all of its health levels, it is hurled deep into the underworld to face destruction.",
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Willpower point",
    "dicePoolText": "Manipulation Streetwise",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Manipulation",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Streetwise",
    "actionText": "Spread your Vitae around the area of the haunt, or onto the object you tie a spirit to.",
    "castingDuration": "1 minute",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The place the necromancer attempted to bind the ghost to become an anathema to them, all attempts to use necromancy in that area are done at -4 dice or result in attacks from Shades.",
    "failureText": "The Shade laughs then eats another peanut.",
    "successText": "Each success ties the Shade to a particular spot of the necromancer's choosing for a night. With the expenditure of a Willpower point the effect lasts an additional week. Expenditure of a point of permanent Willpower extends the duration to a year and a day.",
    "notes": "Prerequisite: You must first have Summon Soul before you can purchase this ritual. And you must first Summon a Shade before you can use any of this ritual.",
    "sourcePage": 225
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Torment",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "It is through the use of this power that elder necromancers convince bound ghosts to behave — or else. Torment allows the vampire to strike a Shade as if he himself were in the lands of the dead, inflicting damages on the wraiths ectoplasmic form. The vampire remains in the real world, however, so he cannot be struck in return.",
