  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "The Ties That Bind",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "The vampire is able to bind a soul to a recently dead corpse and has utter command over it. Note that the corpse is not very sturdy and has no ability to repair its self. However while possessed the ghost can act with all its acumen and use the body as if it were naturally its own.",
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Willpower point + 5 Blood",
    "dicePoolText": "Intelligence 4 Persuasion",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Intelligence",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Persuasion",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "duration": "1 Night 1 per extra Willpower point spent.",
    "castingDuration": "5 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The shade is pushed aside as another more powerful and malevolent entity takes its place. The newly possessed will then try to gain control over the necromancer by any means possible, in order to possess a far superior shell.",
    "failureText": "It's Alive! No, wait... still dead...",
    "successText": "The necromancer has successfully bound the shade to the corpse and it is able to act with all its mental faculties it may have once had plus the general physical attributes the body can offer. This however is not a simple process. The ritual to guide the soul to the body and the shades time in the underworld will have changed it irrevocably. Even if the shades death was recent. The shade will have come back with an additional Dementation from its time in the land of the dead, one that relates to its death and assumed afterlife. This Dementation will affect its every action and thought, as it tries to cope with being back in the realm of the living. Also keep in mind the corpse is still just a corpse. It lacks any ability to heal or grow. It will decompose at the normal rate, until it cannot hold itself together under any kind of movement. If the duration the shade can be bound to the corpse is still active, the condition of the corpse does not matter and the shade will remain bound, however the body may not be in any condition to do anything more than lie there as a pile of bones. Oddly enough it can always speak in ghostly tones, regardless of the corpse's condition...",
    "notes": "Prerequisite: You must first have Summon Soul before you can purchase this ritual. And you must first Summon a Shade before you can use any of this ritual.",
    "sourcePage": 225
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Soul Trap",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "The most feared power of the Necromancer — the ability to capture a Shade, and bind it to a ruby.",
    "vitaeCost": 3,
    "costText": "3 Vitae 4 | Willpower (this Willpower is not recovered until the Shade is let free.)",
    "dicePoolText": "Resolve + Crafts",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Resolve",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Crafts",
    "actionText": "The Necromancer is able to use a ruby of at least 7 mm x mm in size. They cut their palm, have a mortal spit into their bloody hand. The necromancer then places the ruby into their blood and spittle hand and then breathes across their palm.",
    "castingDuration": "A few minutes",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The Shade lashes out in terror and anger at the Necromancer, the mortal who spit is murdered as their soul is devoured by the Shade, granting it +1 Pathos, and then the Shade attacks the Necromancer.",
    "failureText": "The laughter of the dead chills even the coldest heat.",
    "successText": "The Necromancer has bound the Shade to the gem. From that point on, the gem is now its Fetter. And anytime the Shade is not summoned it returns to the gem. As well if it is reduced to 0 Pathos it returns to the gem instead of being destroyed (at the expenditure of 1 Willpower the necromancer can summon the O Pathos Shade, restoring it to I Pathos). The Shade can only be set free by shattering the gem (in which case the Necromancers Willpower point can be regained).",
    "notes": "Prerequisite: You must first have Summon Soul before you can purchase this ritual. And you must first Summon a Shade before you can use any of this ritual.",
    "sourcePage": 226
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Sever Thread",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "The most gruesome and one the most feared powers of the Magi. This ability allows the caster to sever a mortal's tie to his body, leaving their soul to drift in limbo in this world and their body to rot and decay.",
    "vitaeCost": 3,
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "3 Vitae + 1 Willpower",
