    "sourcePage": 226
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Song of the Morrigan",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "The vampire chants, weaving unheard words into the song and instilling an unhealthy fascination with death in his listener. Afflicted individuals find themselves drawn to lonely, inauspicious places as they sink into depression; mortality concerns them as never before and they see ill omens everywhere. If affected by this power for an extended period, mortals go mad and become suicidal, while vampires eventually succumb to torpor.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Manipulation -k Empathy — target's Resolve",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Manipulation",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Empathy",
    "actionText": "The vampire chants to the victim the promises of loss and suffering from all eras.",
    "castingDuration": "I Hour per day target is to be affected.",
    "dramaticFailureText": "A botch indicates the magi affects himself as though he had gained successes equal to the Is rolled.",
    "failureText": "I think that lady is a witch...",
    "successText": "For a number of nights equal to the successes rolled, the target suffers a Compel of depression or morbid anxiety. In addition to the normal effects of a Compel, if a target suffers the effects of this power for more continuous nights than her permanent Resolve, she loses 1 point of Willpower. This cycle continues for each increment of their Resolve. Once a character drops to zero Willpower, she commits suicide (if living) or falls into Torpor (if a vampire). If the power is inten-upted for at least one night, the victim will not suffer death or Torpor no matter how many nights they then suffer this.",
    "sourcePage": 226
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Bastone Del Diavolo",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "Bindings to the world of the living impress an emotional hunger upon Shades. Where they do not need to feed on blood as a vampire does, they still crave the passions of the living. Sacrificing a mortal in the name of your shade feeds this hunger.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "The necromancer must sever the leg of a living mortal, remove the femur from the surrounding tissue, and submerge it in boiling lead. Once the lead has cooled, she inscribes the femur with a litany of curses. Once she has finished her craftsmanship, she must beat the mortal to death with his own femur. She then summons a shade and passes the Bastone through its form.",
    "castingDuration": "The time it takes to complete the above action.",
    "successText": "Increase the permanent Pathos by I as long as the bone is not destroyed.",
    "sourcePage": 226
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Shambling Hordes",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "Shambling Hordes creates exactly what you might think: reanimated corpses with the ability to attack, albeit not very well or very quickly. Each corpse is made from a single body, parts may not be stitched back on.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Willpower + 1 Vitae for each cadaver",
    "dicePoolText": "Stamina + Academics",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Stamina",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Academics",
    "actionText": "Find a fresh corpse - you in theory could use an older one, but the more rotted, the less functional - and find clean, bare skin. Slice your fingers to draw blood, and draw it along the corpse, bidding it rise at the end.",
    "castingDuration": "1 minute per cadaver",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The corpses rise all right, but they take no commands from you or anyone. They seek only to devour anything that has any semblance of human or animal life. They will not stop until utterly destroyed. The necromancer is unable to even relinquish the power.",
    "failureText": "I've got a lovely bunch of corpses didly deet da dee...",
    "successText": "The point of willpower prevents the corpses from rotting much further. However even a fresh corpse will still age and rot to a degree as to be totally recognizable as a corpse. Once created the necromancer will not be able to re-fill those spent Vitae until the cadaver is destroyed or the vampire relinquishes the power, rendering all the Cadavers no more than unanimated dead flesh. Otherwise the cadaver will wait or attempt to carry out its command to the best of its brain dead ability. Any complex commands will not be followed in any recognizable manner. Commands should be concise and specific.\n\nOnce empowered, the corpses wait - for years, if necessary - to fulfill the command given them. The orders might be to protect certain site or simply to attack immediately, but they will be carried out until every last one of the decomposing monsters is destroyed. Cadaver Stats * :",
    "notes": "Strength Charisma none Stamina • Intelligence none Dexterityt Manipu ation none Perception • Resolve none Wits Resolve • • Health 10\n\nSkills: All other skills - none Brawl\n\nCadavers always act last in combat each turn with one action each. They never attempt to dodge. Cadavers have O Willpower, however are treated as 10 Willpower to defend against attacks that target Willpower. They are not affected by Wounds. Cadavers use the same Fire damage ru es as Vampires. Cadavers cannot use weapons or manipulate simple mechanisms like gun triggers or door knobs.",
    "sourcePage": 227
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Hybrid",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "This is a further mastery of the Shambling Hordes power. Now the necromancer may stitch together bodies which will have appropriate attributes however they are built. This is not limited to human body parts. The quality of the stitching should be decent, however, once the power takes effect the parts will bond together and function as if they had always been attached.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae per limb, 2 if non-human",
    "dicePoolText": "Dexterity + Crafts",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Dexterity",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Crafts",
    "actionText": "Using cat gut string soaked in you blood to stitch body parts.",
    "castingDuration": "The time it takes to stitch the part.",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The string breaks and that location of the Cadaver becomes too frayed to ever have anything stitched to it again.",
    "failureText": "Over and over or Lembert stitch? Can't decide...",
    "successText": "The cadaver gains the ability to use the limb as if it were natural part of their body. The ST may impose penalties on Cadaver actions if the limbs are poorly matched to the cadaver's size or shape.",
    "notes": "Prerequisite: You must first have Shambling Hordes before you can purchase this ritual. And you must first successfully create a Cadaver before you can use any of this ritual.",
    "sourcePage": 227
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Lilliputian",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "Necromancers use this ritual to create spies and stalkers out of body parts such as hands or skulls, or small dead animals like rats or foxes.",
    "vitaeCost": 3,
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "3 Vitae + 1 Willpower",
    "dicePoolText": "Resolve Arts",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Resolve",
    "actionText": "The required body part or animal carcass, the weapon used to sever/kill it, a small concoction of urine, fecal matter, and semen. The caster coats a blade (or other device suited to the task) in a cocktail of bodily fluids, and uses it to cut the targeted appendage off its root limb or body, or kills the small animal (which cannot be larger than a small dog and cannot fly, regardless of whether it has wings).",
    "castingDuration": "The times it takes to complete the above action.",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The spirit of the victim flares in its death, doing number of unsoakable Lethal damage to the necromancer equal to the number of I's rolled.",
    "failureText": "Maybe I should stick to Legos...",
    "successText": "After massaging vitae into the target, it comes to life as small servant, unfailingly loyal to its master. The Lilliputian can scale walls, hop (even if it lacks the limbs to do so), and hide effectively. While it cannot speak or perform tasks requiring deep thought, it can telepathically communicate single images to its creator. If it strays farther than 100 yards/ meters from the vampire, it falls inert, only awakening again once the vampire enters that range. All of this is done at a dice pool equal to the necromancers' Blood Potency. The Lilliputian remains functional forever and does not additionally decay. If the necromancer falls into torpor, it can spend 1 Willpower to still communicate and command its Lilliputian. A Lilliputian can only take 5 points of Bashing or Lethal damage before it's utterly destroyed. Any amount of aggravated destroys it. It is as susceptible to Fire as vampires are.",
    "sourcePage": 228
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Tremens",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "'He rose to speak for not one but the dance of two Kings two men ofdifferent moment different weight in the eyes, the memory of God\n\nOne danced at the sense of joy the feeling ofwonder, happiness The other danced the dance of death, miserable as his life spun Macabre",
    "willpowerCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Willpower point",
    "dicePoolText": "Manipulation + Subterfuge",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Manipulation",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Subterfuge",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "duration": "The number of successes the necromancer achieved over her target is the number of rounds (or minutes if not in combat) he has control over the undead. At the end of that time, the necromancer may spend 2 Vitae to force another contested roll.",
    "castingDuration": "2 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "Your body is flung into convulsions, as the feeling of a dozen threads seem to tug at you in every direction, painful and debilitating. You flail about for 1 minute per botch die.",
    "failureText": "Do you like puppet shows? No? Oh...",
    "successText": "You are able to puppet the body of any walking dead. Be it cadaver, vampire or promethean or whatever. This is not limited to humans, however the body can only perform the functions it is able. Thus a puppeteer can move a vampire-marionette as he wishes, and even make him spend Vitae or use his Disciplines. He cannot induce a Dominion roll, however he can put the vampire-marionette in a situation that will cause him to test for Dominion.",
    "sourcePage": 228
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Rigor Mortis",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "The necromancer induces rigor mortis in a vampire.",
    "costText": "1 to 5 Blood",
    "dicePoolText": "Stamina -k Persuasion",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Stamina",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Persuasion",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "duration": "The number of successes the necromancer achieved over her target is the number of minutes the target is affected. A victim may spend blood points equal I for 1 minute in order to recover, but this must be followed with a Dominion roll.",
    "castingDuration": "2 seconds",
    "dramaticFailureText": "None",
    "failureText": "None",
    "successText": "Victims so affected lose 3 dots in Dexterity (to a mimumum of O), and are in such pain that using mental Disciplines requires a roll of Resolve. If their Dextrerity is reduced to 0, then they are utterly immbobile but not in Torpoer. If the victim moves violently in a given turn while affected, she takes 1 level of Lethal damage that cannot be soaked.",
    "sourcePage": 229
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Insight",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "This power allows a necromancer to stare into the eyes of a corpse and see reflected there the last thing the dead man witnessed. The vision only appears in the eyes of a cadaver and in visible to no one except the necromancer using Insight.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Perception -k Intrigue",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Perception",
    "dicePoolSkill": "Intrigue",
    "actionText": "<insert how to use the blood in a ritual>>",
    "castingDuration": "1 second",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The images burn themselves into the necromancers mind, and he cannot forget them, nor can he make them out to any degree of understanding.",
    "failureText": "She had such beautiful eyes...",
    "successText": "As the vampire stares into the targets eyes the number of successes determines the clarity of the vision.\n\n1-2 successes fuzzy sense of the subjects death",
    "notes": "3-4 successes clear image, with sound, of the minutes preceding death\n\nsuccesses Full sensory perception of the hour leading up to the target's death",
    "sourcePage": 229
  },
  {
    "group": "Necromancy",
    "name": "Din of the Damned",
    "category": "Rituals",
    "flavor": "This ritual seals any space against attempts at eavesdropping via either supernatural or mundane means.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "None",
    "actionText": "The necromancer draws an unbroken line of ashes on the ground.",
    "castingDuration": "A few moments to expertly create the line of ashes.",
    "successText": "So long as the line remains unbroken, no one outside of the line can hear anything going on inside. 03",
    "sourcePage": 229
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Ritual of Passing",
    "flavor": "This is something done on a regular basis. No Sabbat ritae may be used unless this Ritual of Passing has been performed within the past 3 nights.\n\nIt is a rededication to the faith performed as an hour long ritual in which ashes of a dead mortal human are burned along with sheep caul fat and lilies of the field (other incense is often added due to the smell). As the smoke rises the prayer must be spoken and repeated until the hour is out.\n\nFrom our place in Nod we rose, and wrapped in our funeral shroud still we walk Blessed Children of Brother Caine, from whom all unlife flows, We, who walk in the moonlight, and spread your Wicked words\n\nTo Heaven, we will not go To Hell, we will not go Only upon this Earth will we remain And from God's side we leave, to stay forever from His Light And to your side, Brother Caine\n\nWaste not our second chance Waste not your Blessing, the Blood of the Second Sin In Death do we remain",
    "sourcePage": 234
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Coterie",
    "flavor": "Available only by performing this ritae with members of your own Coven, Coterie pulls on the bonds formed.",
    "actionText": "Each vampire in the coven drinks 1 point of Vitae from the other in utter darkness (no light of any sort may exist within 20 feet of those performing the ritual, even if that light is through walls, below ground or from the moon or a single dim light). For the remainder of the evening blood may be spend to activate this ritual.",
    "successText": "By spending 1 Vitae, the vampire can interact empathically with all other vampires within their Coven who have also drank from you this night. This has the following benefits:",
    "notes": "communal pool of bonus dice is established, with one die added for each participant. Additional dice may be added for each additional Vitae spent. Each may take dice from this pool as needed. The dice pools lasts until it is used up or the scene is over.\n\nTrying to gain the element of surprise is a lost cause. Once one of the Coven sees someone sneaking up on them, all of them know.\n\nBy concentrating on a coven-mate, the vampire may loan any of her Skills to her. She may take no other action while doing this. This does not apply to disciplines.\n\nIf another vampire wishes to use mental Disciplines on a coven-member, the difficulty is determined with the highest Resolve in the Coven. If successful, the Coven is not affected, only that vampire is affected.\n\nFighting maneuvers that normally require very detailed choreography, such as acrobatics, can be done with no minuses due to their complexity at all, regardless if practiced or not.",
    "sourcePage": 234
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Vaulderie",
    "flavor": "The Vaulderie defines the Sabbat as a group. Vampires who partake show that they are part of the sect; vampires who refuse the cup can never really belong. The Blood Bond, as Camarilla and independent vampires use it, binds the subject as the slave of his regnant. It reinforces the static hierarchy of elder over childe. The Vaulderie makes the participants equal, uniting them in their shared cause. You may only perform the Vaulderie with members of your own Coven as well as the presiding Ensik.",
    "actionText": "Simply mixing vitae isn't sufficient for the Vaulderie. The presiding Ensik must use a cutting tool and cup dedicated to this specific purpose. Ensik's generally decorate their tools with hieroglyphics and artwork that expresses their faith and Road. The priest takes her ritual tools, makes a cut in herself and drains out as much blood as she cares to contribute. Once the Ensik begins the ceremony, she passes the cup and tool to each participant in turn, who contributes as much blood as each chooses. Contributing only one vitae looks bad-do you have something to hide? Contributing five or more vitae, except when duty requires, looks bad, too - are you angling for control?",
    "successText": "Once you have created the Vaulderie bond with your coven all Blood Bonds are broken and a Coven is formed. The only way to break a Vaulderie is for all of the surviving members of your Coven to suffer final death. There is no end to the Vaulderie, and Vaulderie bonds don't erode.\n\nYou inherently know if any of your coven members have suffered Final Death, though not why or from what. You know the moment it happens, regardless of distance or time of day.\n\nWhile you are in the presence of your Coven mates, you may use up to 1 point of Vitae from one of the other members. You do not need to be in physical contact, and the action does not require their consent. You may not spend this vitae if it would reduce their pool to I or less. You may pull an additional amount of vitae per member of your coven, up to 6. This can come from one member in your presence or pulled from multiples in your area.",
    "notes": "Trying to put in someone else's blood, from a concealed pouch or other source, doesn't work. The cup erupts and splashes the blood everywhere. Everyone loses the blood they put in. The Ensik must start the ritual again, and the offender probably faces swift destruction.\n\nThe Ensik takes the filled cup and performs a simple ritual over it that merges the blood together. Only a clergy member of the Sabbat may perform this ritae, and must be at least of rank Ensik. Even if the priest was chosen on the spur of the moment by coven mates interested in creating their Vinculum, an Ensik performing the ritual makes it work while someone not of the faith could perform the same ritual but get no results. The Ensik offers a brief blessing on each participant as she drinks from the cup. The ritual gives back to each participant I vitae.\n\nEvery Sabbat member takes the Vaulderie seriously. Even the most feral wanderers or rowdy urban punks settle down for this ritual even if they're never serious at any other time. This is what it's all about. Each vampire takes away from the ritual a special bond to all other members of the coven.\n\ncharacter attempting to destroy another vampire to whom he has any Vinculum rating at all must spend 2 Willpower points. Acting less terminally against the interests of a vampire to whom he has a Vinculum requires spending 1 Willpower point. The only exception is Monomacy performed under the supervision of an approved Sabbat clergy.",
    "sourcePage": 235
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Aeramentum",
    "flavor": "This power was developed as a means to test a foe's might. By merely tasting the blood of his subject, the Cainite can determine how much vitae remains in the subject, if the subject is a vampire, how recently he has fed, his approximate generation, and with enough successes if the vampire has committed Diablerie. The blood must be fresh or at least not totally dried to use this ability.",
    "vitaeCost": 1,
    "costText": "1 Vitae",
    "dicePoolText": "Perception + Sacraments",
    "dicePoolAttribute": "Perception",
    "dramaticFailureText": "The vampire using this power gains a minor dementia lasting for one scene in which they become obsessed with tasting the subject blood once again, until it's all gone, and if gone and the scene continues, they must go find their subject and feed..",
    "failureText": "A moment's sticky yet ashy taste of iron and salt on your tongue",
    "successText": "The number of successes on the roll determines the details of the information they gleaned. Successes Information Examples",
    "notes": "Action: Instant\n\n1 Fragmented details, hints at truths but nothing assured\n\n3 The details are clearer, and the vampire gleans insight on the subject's physical condition\n\n5 The details tell the whole story of the subject, their age, their powers and their physical condition and distance from the Magi.",
    "sourcePage": 235
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Animus",
    "flavor": "There are three wisdoms of Caine written in the Erciyes Fragments allude to a triptych of vampire being. Chief amongst these three is the Beast which dwells within all Cainites. It was by faith this rite was perfected, and it is by devotion that it can be used. Used to summon your Beast forth as a spirit of vengeance which acts like a paranormal demon to haunt and destroy your enemy.",
    "actionText": "First you must have completed the Sabbat ritual of Passing within the past 3 nights. The magi must make a white death mask anew each time and wear it as they cast the ritual. They then slit each wrist with a deep wound such that it will drain much of their blood. Holding their wrists above their head they look up into the pour of blood, and chant the unholy incantations of the Prayer of the Spirit as blood drips upon the mask. Upon speaking the words, the bloody death mask goes from bone white to charcoal black. They may then end the flow of blood. Then, slowly removing the mask from their face and placing it to face them, they say the Prayer of Twisted Knots, summoning forth their beast as a manifest spirit of vengeance.",
    "successText": "For a number of days per success, the spirit of vengeance is summoned from your spilt blood. While it is active it will attempt to complete one of the following tasks you command of it:",
    "notes": "Roll Resolve + Status (Sabbat). If the roll is a success then the spirit may be commanded as below. If you gain no successes or botch, then the spirit turns upon its master and savagely tears into them doing I wound of Lethal damage equal to the character's dots in Blood Potency and then dissipates into nothing.\n\nKill someone\n\nDestroy something\n\nHarass someone specific\n\nHarass anyone in one area the size of a house\n\nThis dark spirit cannot be seen except for a ghostly waver to its form — usually when it goes to strike. It makes noise only to scare or startle its prey — a sound that is utterly inhuman, horrifying, and loud. It can pass through walls and will follow its prey as fast as a man can run but no faster. It is only active at night, and can only be harmed or banished at night.\n\nWhen it goes to affect the world it gets a dice pool of 1 die for every point of blood you spent when slitting your wrists, plus your dots in Resolve. It can only be destroyed by taking enough fire damage in a single strike equal to its dice pool (anything less will merely cause it to flee from the fire).\n\nBlood Sorcery user can banish it by casting a banishment spell needing more successes than the spirit's dice pool (this is an extended roll).\n\nWhile the spirit is active you may not use any Disciplines, but you can use Blood Sorcery or Ritae as normal.\n\nSevenfold vengeance, if someone harm you, you gain a pool of 7 successes for whatever roll you want to add them to (you may add or more, up to all 7 in a single roll if you wish). Once spent they are gone.\n\nYou can banish the spirit away at any time at will.\n\nHow to Learn It You must be taught the Sabbat Prayer of the Spirit.\n\nOh Angel of the spurned Oh Angel of the vengeful Oh Angel of Rage Who flies through our Souls as in the skies\n\nWe behold You as Ourselves May we be as You are And carry your Vengeance within us To use as You used To wash our feet in the blood of the Wicked Until Caine deems us un worthy",
    "sourcePage": 236
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Corpus",
    "flavor": "Second of the wisdoms of Caine found in the Erciyes Fragments is the lesson of flesh. Therein is says only three remnants of the once mortal you were. The Beast you invited in, the blood which flows and the body which remains. The flesh binds the Beast to the Blood. And this junction can be made powerful when both are called upon.",
    "actionText": "First you must have completed the Sabbat ritual of Passing within the past 3 nights. The vampire must have a very sharp knife, or better yet - a scalpel. Then with the precision only the dead could wield, they will inscribe the Prayers of the Eternal Form upon their flesh, covering their body from ankles to their neck and wrists.",
    "successText": "You may spend blood for Fortitude, Celerity, and Potence beyond your Attribute limits to a maximum of 5 dots. You also may heal an additional point of Lethal or Aggravated per blood spent. Your blood capacity is increased by I for each day you participated in the Feast of Solomon prior to petforming this rite, up to a max of +10. You can ignore the Staked status by spending point of Willpower to make a single action (likely to remove the stake).\n\nHow to Learn It You must be taught the Prayer of the Eternal Form.\n\nBefore A Braham, We were Before David, We were Before the Son, We were And so shall We be, outliving God's creations\n\nAnd by Caine, We walk By Darkness, We walk Under the cloak of stars We call our Nights For We are the Creature that haunts The Beast that stalks By the blessing of Caine, until the Day takes us",
    "notes": "Roll Dexterity + Status (Sabbat). On a success you gain the benefits from below.",
    "sourcePage": 237
  },
  {
    "group": "Auctoritas",
    "name": "Cruor",
    "flavor": "By using the power of vitae to cleanse and restore, the Cainite releases her blood, allowing it to wash over another and carry away spiritual impurities from outside influences. This power cleanses the target's soul, purging his mind of externally imposed supernatural taints and stains.",
    "actionText": "The leading member of this ritae baptizes the forehead of the intended subject with one blood point, then places her hands on his head. Both parties spend a minimum of one minute in deep concentration chanting the medi tative mantras of Darkest Hour.",
    "successText": "To erase current and ongoing influences from are: Dominate, Dementation, Presence, or similar effects , the invoker spends a number of Vitae equal to the Blood Potency of the one who inflictedit for one supernatural mind influencing power he wishes to nullify. After the hour is up, it removes the effects of that power. This does not shield the subject from or ward him against those powers in the future.\n\nIt can also be used to clear a cainite's mind when they are suffering Dominion. The invoker of this ritae must spend I vitae roll Resolve + Empathy, on an Extended roll until they get equal to or more successes than the cainite suffering Dominion has in Blood Potency.\n\nAs well this ritae can be used to clear a vampires emotions of Bloodthirst Compels. The chanter need only spend 1 Vitae and gain successes on a Resolve + Empathy roll equal to or greater than the Compel value.\n\nHow to Learn It You must be taught the meditative mantras of Darkest Hour while under the influence of some such mental or emotional effect, or Dominion or Bloodthirst Compels. Your guiding priest teaches you both mental and verbal components to clear your mind, until you have done so six times, over six days. These are extended sounds and simple body positions held in place as you repeat the secret words of Darkest Hour.",
    "sourcePage": 237
  },
  {
    "group": "Ignobilis",
    "name": "Immolatio",
    "flavor": "By sacrificing a mortal human, the Cainite can spill the blood of their foes. This ritae allows the Cainite to force another vampire to spend blood against his will.",
    "actionText": "The sabbatist finds a living mortal in the likeness of their foe. They use mirrored kris-like curved knife and carve the symbol of Abel's Lament upon their victim, cutting them deep enough to let blood flow freely while they say the inverted name of their foe.",
    "successText": "Each success causes 1 point of blood drained from the victim to bleed from the eyes and orifices of their foe. Failure means your faith was not strong enough and you must wait a full night before you can try again. A Botch indicates you become lost in the bloodletting and suffer the effects of this ritae, losing 1 vitae for each botch die — then you roll for Dominion. If not botched, the roll may be made over and over until the victim is bled to death (typically about 8 points of blood).\n\nRoll Manipulation + Empathy + Merit: Status (Sabbat) minus the target's Resolve\n\nHow to Learn It Cainite must be brought in by an Apostolic who will teach them to read and understand the protected chapters of the Book of Nod which detail Caine's sacrifice of his brother and process by which he used.",
    "notes": "Book of Nod Chronicles of Sahih I Chapter 3 Versus 11 - 16\n\nII(Begin by) stripping the victim of his ornaments, stretching him over the convex sacrificial stones and while fare priests held his arms, legs, head, 12the high priests cut open his breast with a mirrored knife, and tore out the heart. 13This was held up to the night sky to provide the land of Nod with nourishment, before it was cast into a basin of Copa placed in a position to enable the blood and incense to ascend to God. 14 The body was hurled down the steps of the temple to the court where it was seized by the priest or by the warrior who captured the victim. 15 Who then brought it to a solemn feast was then held on the flesh, the skin having first been removed to be worn ceremonially by men who seem to have acquired thereby the fertilizing the land with health-giving qualities of the sacrifice. 16Some of the blood was carried back to the temple and smeared on the hips of the images of goats.",
    "sourcePage": 238
  },
  {
    "group": "Ignobilis",
    "name": "Lemniscus",
    "flavor": "With the power of this ritual, a vampire may temporarily intenupr the reanimating effect of vampiric Vitae, rendering a vampire immobile as the stiffening of muscles common to dead bodies takes hold.",
    "actionText": "The vampire must have come into contact with the victim's blood previously. Then only needing to see their target, they make a motion as if binding a ribbon or rope about their own wrist.",
    "successText": "Make the roll and the number of successes determines the amount of dice penalty the victim suffers to any physical action they take during the scene. For all actions the victim is at a 0 die pool or less, their body acts stiff as the dead, and they are helplessly immobile. Number of successes are halved against the living. If using a Sacrament, you may spend up to 3 Vitae to drench the sacrament in your blood to gain 1 die per Vitae on your roll.\n\nRoll Resolve + Subterfuge minus target's Wits\n\nHow to Learn It The ties that bind all cainites are through the blood. How much more powerful then can this ritae be when blood is known and spilt. Taught only by the Mand'rite black priests of the Sabbat, whereupon they teach you the true state of death. You willingly place yourself in a state of Torpor while the Mandrite chants the words of the angel Uriel as they drip their blood into your dead dry maw. You awake, but three times you must do this, such that the chants penneate your torpor dreams, and when you rise the final time, you can complete the final phrase.\n\nRepeated by the priest Dies illa Solvet saeculum in favi/la Quan tus tremor est futurus\n\nQuando iudex est ven turus Cuncta stricte discussurus Tuba mirum spalgens sonum\n\nPer sepulcra region um Coget omnes ante thronum MOIS stupebit et natura\n\nCum resurget creaana ludican ti responsura Confutatis maledictis\n\nCompleted by the supplicant Flammis acribus addictis Oro supplex et acclinis Cor contritum quasi Cinis",
    "sourcePage": 238
  },
  {
    "group": "Ignobilis",
    "name": "Furtum",
    "flavor": "Cainite using this power siphons vitae from his victims.",
    "actionText": "No contact is needed, though a clear line of sight is required and they must be within 30ft. Blood literally streams out in an ethereal form, yet still crimson red, into the sabbatist's mouth.",
    "successText": "Each success steals one point of Vitae from his victim, transferring it to the Cainite. Vitae stolen in this manner does not count towards Blood Bonding.\n\nRoll Resolve + Persuasion minus target's Stamina\n\nIf using a sacrament of a jar, then whisper the name of the target into the jar and close it spending 1 point of Willpower. Upon opening the jar while looking at your target the link is far stronger. Each second you hold the jar open, it drains the amount of Vitae this ritae normally would. This causes the vitae to flow into the jar instead of your mouth. Once the jar is closed, the ritae is complete and blood stops draining. Regardless of how much vitae was drained, the jar only contains a number of vitae equal to successes rolled.\n\nHow to Learn It gathering led by a Praecipuus of a specific order is held at a crossroads in honor of Caine, wanderer of crossroads and transformation. A circle of black candles (the Praecipuus's candle is white) is placed around the edges of the crossroads — one for each participant. The sabbatists enter the circle as one, standing at its inner edge until everyone is around it. Each then takes a candle in turn and extinguishes it with a point of their Vitae, saying what they (spiritually) offer to their Road). The candle is then set in the center of the circle. Each candle, once set in the center, creates a circle of candles. The white and last candle of the Praecipuus goes in the center of candles as they finish with a blessing of wisdom for all those walking the land of Nod, \"May your trod in darkness find your way to Caine's light. For his truth of blood is yours to keep and to call upon.\"",
    "sourcePage": 239
  },
  {
    "group": "Ignobilis",
    "name": "Rite of the Slain and Risen",
    "flavor": "One of the most feared ritae of the Sword of Caine sabbatists, this allows you to devour another vampire in Diablerie with no chance of addiction.",
    "actionText": "You contact a Praecipuus who if approving of your mark, makes contact with an affiliated Apostolic, who names the victim that you intend to diablerize. The Praecipuus, with three other participants who know the ritual, then leads everyone in a one-hour group ceremony. All don robes and masks to ceremonially re-enact the First Destruction as told in the Book of Nod; taking the parts of Caine (You) holding a cup o/ your blood, Ea (Praecipuus) sounding a deep resonant drum, Sarani (Apostolic) chanting the incantations, and the chosen Children (3 additional participants) each holding a symbol of their Road through Nod made from pure silver as they repeat phrases of the incantations.",
    "notes": "Then the beneficiary diablerizes his specified target just before the sunrise, the victim's sire, all of the sire's and the victim's childer, and any vampire holding a Blood Bond with the victim share her final sensations as she perishes. Each affected subject loses 1 Vitae and 1 Willpower point, which go to the diablerist (this cannot exceed maximums). If the diablerist's blood pool and Willpower are full, the remainder goes to the vizier, and following that, to the sorcerer. Furthermore, all of these collateral targets lose 1 point of Willpower for every 10 minutes they spend in the presence of the diablerist, the vizier, or the sorcerer due to suffering flashbacks of the original victim's demise. This effect lasts for 7 nights.\n\nHow it's Works No roll is needed. The power comes from the dictates of Caine himself, to reclaim the blood he graced to the world from those who are so unworthy. You do still, however, roll for Theft of Disciplines as per Diablerie rules.\n\nHow to Learn It You must be inducted into the order of the Sword of Caine. Should you pass their trials and join them, it is taught as a matter of requirement. See the Sword of Caine for details.",
    "sourcePage": 239
  },
